# Module-owned documentation, copied into the site's tree by
# `pnpm --filter backend run composer:generate` (feature 100 Phase 2, FR-016).
#
# The source of every one of these pages is the `docs/` layer of the module that
# owns it, and committing the copy would put 10,311 lines of prose in this
# repository twice — one editable copy and one that looks editable and is not.
# A **tracked** file is never ignored whatever the pattern says, so the pages
# that genuinely live in the site's own tree stay visible here and no list of
# exceptions is written down: git's own answer to "is this file this
# repository's" is the discriminator, and it cannot go stale.
#
# `git add` a new page that really belongs to the site rather than to a module.
/docs/docs/modules/**
/docs/.module-docs-copies.json

# The fixture instances `admin/test/unit/shell-theme-override.test.ts` builds
# (feature 110, T126).
#
# Ignored rather than merely removed afterwards, and the reason is Tailwind's:
# the fixture sits under `admin/`, which is the admin's own automatic-detection
# base, so a tracked one would compile its classes into this repository's admin
# bundle. An ignored path is skipped by that walk and is still scanned in full by
# the fixture's *own* build, whose base is the fixture directory — the ignore
# rules apply to a base's descendants relative to that base
# (`admin-stylesheet-composition.md` §1).
/admin/.instance-theme-fixture/
